<p>I have corrected the description in the Info Bar of your article (<a href="/scp-4322">SCP-4322</a>, <a href="/scp-4339">SCP-4339</a>, <a href="/scp-3597">SCP-3597</a>, <a href="/scp-4781">SCP-4781</a>). It is necessary to make it work properly. However, when I looked at the editing history after that, I realized the possibility that you intentionally made them not work.</p>
<p>This section explains how to delete &quot;Translations:&quot; correctly.</p>
<p>1. Move the Info Bar include statement to top of the page source. This is a necessary process.</p>
<p>2. Add the following code in <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">[[module&#32;CSS]]</span>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>.translation_block {<br />
display:none;<br />
}</p>
</blockquote>
<p>3. Now you can remove the display of &quot;Translations:&quot;!</p>

